data: {"delta":"Based on the retrieved evidence, here's the current status of Node.js versions:\n\n**LTS Line:**\n- Node.js 26 (Lithium) is the current LTS version\n- The first LTS release in this line was Node.js 26.13.0, released on October 28, 2026\n- This version will be supported until the end of April 2029\n\n**Current Line:**\n- Node.js 26.10.0 is the most recent Current version, released on September 22, 2026\n- Starting with Node.js 27, the project will switch to one major release per year, with each reaching LTS after spending half a year as Current\n\nNote that Node.js 24 left Active LTS on October 20, 2026, and is no longer in the active support phase.","conversationId":"cmw02v8yy000zqapy21ruljf6"}

